---
const total = 28799;
const groups = (
  [
    ['Republican primary', 10262, 'rep'],
    ['Democratic primary', 9398, 'dem'],
    ['General election only', 6666, 'gen'],
    ['No primary history', 2473, 'none'],
  ] as const
).map(([name, count, tone]) => ({
  name,
  count,
  tone,
  percent: `${Math.round((count / total) * 1000) / 10}%`,
  share: (count / total) * 100,
}));
---

<section class="early-vote" aria-labelledby="early-vote-title">
  <h2 id="early-vote-title">Early voting</h2>
  <p>
    Through October 30: 28,799 ballots, 27,611 in person and 1,188 by mail.
    The party lines are earlier primary records of those voters, not votes for a party on this ballot.
    Someone who has voted in both primaries is counted with the party of the most recent one.
    Secretary of State report updated November 2 at 10:05 a.m.,
    <a class="text-link" href="https://turnout.transparencyusa.org/2026-general/county/bastrop/" rel="noopener">posted by Transparency USA</a>.
    The county results file still shows no ballots.
    <a class="text-link" href="https://www.bastropvotes.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Press-Release_Election-Results.pdf" rel="noopener">The elections office</a>
    will release early-voting totals after the last voter has voted.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {groups.map((group) => (
      <li>
        <span class="who">{group.name}</span>
        <span class="track">
          <span class:list={['bar', group.tone]} style={`width:${group.share}%`}></span>
        </span>
        <span class="fig">
          <strong>{group.count.toLocaleString('en-US')}</strong>
          <em>{group.percent}</em>
        </span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</section>

<style>
  .early-vote { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
  .early-vote h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); border-top: 4px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 0.55rem; }
  .early-vote p { max-width: 46rem; margin-top: 0.45rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .early-vote ul { list-style: none; margin: 0.9rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .early-vote li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 12.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center; }
  .who { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .track { display: block; height: 1.35rem; background: var(--paper-2); }
  .bar { display: block; height: 100%; }
  .bar.rep { background: #b42318; }
  .bar.dem { background: #1d4e89; }
  .bar.gen { background: var(--pine); }
  .bar.none { background: #8a8175; }
  .fig { display: flex; gap: 0.45rem; align-items: baseline; justify-content: flex-end; min-width: 7.2rem; }
  .fig strong { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 620; }
  .fig em { font-style: normal; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .early-vote li { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; }
    .who { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
    .fig { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; min-width: 0; }
    .track { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 2; }
  }
</style>
